  "body": "## Summary\nSplitting a permanent veNFT via `multiSplit()` allocates child amounts with floor division and does not reconcile `permanentLockBalance`, causing (1) deterministic rounding loss of locked value and (2) global permanent accounting drift.\n\n## Finding Description\n`multiSplit()` burns the parent veNFT and mints multiple child veNFTs with proportional amounts calculated by integer division. For a parent with amount `A` and weights `w[i]`, each child receives `floor(A * w[i] / Σw)`. This truncation yields Σ(child) ≤ A and usually Σ(child) < A when `A` is not exactly divisible by `Σw`. The parent is first burned and then children are minted, so the rounding remainder is lost on-chain.\n\nWhen the parent is a permanent lock (`originalLocked.isPermanent == true`), `multiSplit()` never adjusts the global `permanentLockBalance` to reflect the (smaller) sum of the new child amounts. As a result, `permanentLockBalance` remains at its pre-split value, while the true sum of permanent child locks is smaller due to rounding. This breaks the invariant that `permanentLockBalance` equals the sum of all permanently locked amounts and contaminates global voting-supply snapshots (via `_checkpoint`, which records `last_point.permanent = permanentLockBalance`).\n\nSecurity guarantees broken:\n- Conservation of locked value in splits: Σ(child amounts) must equal the parent’s amount.\n- Accuracy of global permanent accounting: `permanentLockBalance` must track the real sum of permanent locks to ensure correct supply snapshots and downstream weighting.\n\nRelevant code:\n- Burn parent, checkpoint, and mint children with floor division:\n  - ve33/contracts/VotingEscrow.sol:1162–1189\n- Global permanent included in checkpoints:\n  - ve33/contracts/VotingEscrow.sol:733\n- No permanent reconciliation in `multiSplit`.\n\n## Impact Explanation\nMedium impact:\n- On-chain locked value is lost deterministically (rounding “dust”) upon splitting; users cannot recover it.\n- `permanentLockBalance` becomes larger than the true permanent total, skewing global accounting and analyses that rely on accurate permanent weights (e.g., supply curves, voting snapshots).\n- The drift accumulates each time permanent locks are split, affecting protocol-wide accounting.\n\n## Likelihood Explanation\nHigh likelihood:\n- The behavior is triggered by normal user actions (splitting a permanent veNFT) without special timing or adversarial setup.\n- Any split into ≥2 children under non-divisible allocations produces rounding loss.\n- No safeguards currently adjust `permanentLockBalance` in `multiSplit`.\n\n\n## Recommendation\n- Preserve the parent total exactly:\n  - Compute child amounts for indices 0..N−2 using floor division; set the last child to `parent_amount − Σ(previous_children)` to guarantee Σ(children) == parent.\n- Reconcile `permanentLockBalance` for permanent splits:\n  - If `originalLocked.isPermanent`, first subtract the parent’s amount from `permanentLockBalance`, then add the exact sum of child amounts (with the remainder fix, net change should be zero).\n- Add invariants and events:\n  - After split, assert Σ(child.amount) == original amount (for permanent splits) and emit an event detailing the split distribution to aid verification.\n\nImplementing these changes prevents both rounding loss and permanent accounting drift, keeping per-NFT and global permanent state consistent.",
  "proof_of_concept": "```solidity\n  /// @notice Validates that multiSplit on a permanent veNFT causes rounding loss\n    /// across children and does not reconcile permanentLockBalance, creating\n    /// permanent accounting drift.\n    function test_multisplit_causes_permanent_accounting_drift() external {\n        // Allow splitting by toggling permission (team is this test contract)\n        votingEscrow.toggleSplit(address(this), true);\n\n        // Create a lock with an amount that will induce rounding with weights [1,1,1]\n        uint256 amount = 100; // deliberately small to highlight rounding: 100/3 = 33 each, sum = 99\n        hybr.approve(address(votingEscrow), amount);\n        // lock for at least one epoch (HybraTimeLibrary.WEEK == 1800 in tests). Use 3600 seconds.\n        uint256 tokenId = votingEscrow.create_lock_for(amount, 3600, address(this));\n\n        // Convert to permanent; permanentLockBalance should increase by `amount`\n        votingEscrow.lockPermanent(tokenId);\n        (int128 aBefore,, bool isPerm) = votingEscrow.locked(tokenId);\n        assertTrue(isPerm, \"expected permanent lock\");\n        uint256 originalAmount = uint256(int256(aBefore));\n        assertEq(originalAmount, amount, \"unexpected original amount\");\n        uint256 permBefore = votingEscrow.permanentLockBalance();\n        assertEq(permBefore, amount, \"permanentLockBalance should equal original amount before split\");\n\n        // Perform multisplit with 3 children and weights [1,1,1]\n        uint[] memory weights = new uint[](3);\n        weights[0] = 1; weights[1] = 1; weights[2] = 1;\n        uint256[] memory childIds = votingEscrow.multiSplit(tokenId, weights);\n        assertEq(childIds.length, 3, \"expected 3 child nfts\");\n\n        // Sum children amounts\n        uint256 sumChildren = 0;\n        for (uint i = 0; i < childIds.length; i++) {\n            (int128 childAmt,, bool childPerm) = votingEscrow.locked(childIds[i]);\n            assertTrue(childPerm, \"children should inherit permanent flag\");\n            sumChildren += uint256(int256(childAmt));\n        }\n\n        // Rounding slack must exist: 100 split equally into 3 => 33,33,33 (sum=99)\n        assertLt(sumChildren, originalAmount, \"expected rounding loss across children\");\n\n        // permanentLockBalance was not reconciled in multiSplit; it remains as before\n        uint256 permAfter = votingEscrow.permanentLockBalance();\n        assertEq(permAfter, permBefore, \"permanentLockBalance changed unexpectedly\");\n\n        // Therefore, global permanent accounting now exceeds the true sum across children\n        // (permAfter == originalAmount, sumChildren == originalAmount - 1)\n        assertGt(permAfter, sumChildren, \"expected permanentLockBalance to exceed actual child sum\");\n    }\n```",
